---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="The Bookstand — Motiva Hub" description="Six books we return to. A curated bookstand for the disciplined mind.">
  <section class="bookstand" style="padding-top: 150px;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">The Wisdom Stack</p>
      <h1 class="bp-title">A curated <em>bookstand.</em></h1>
      <p class="premise-sub" style="margin: 0 0 40px;">Six books we return to. Not the year's loudest titles, but the ones that earn their place on the shelf beside the bed.</p>
      <div class="bp-grid">
        <div class="bp-card">
          <p class="bp-meta">Stoicism · c. 180 AD</p>
          <h3>Meditations</h3>
          <p>"The private notebook of an emperor writing to himself. The closest thing we have to a manual for the inner life."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bp-card">
          <p class="bp-meta">Habits · 2018</p>
          <h3>Atomic Habits</h3>
          <p>"A systems thinker's case for identity-based change. The clearest modern argument that you do not rise to your goals — you fall to your systems."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bp-card">
          <p class="bp-meta">Focus · 2016</p>
          <h3>Deep Work</h3>
          <p>"The case for treating concentration as a craft. Newport argues that the ability to focus without distraction is the superpower of the century."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bp-card">
          <p class="bp-meta">Philosophy · 2016</p>
          <h3>The Daily Stoic</h3>
          <p>"Three hundred and sixty-six meditations, one for each day. A practical doorway into a tradition that has guided disciplined minds for two thousand years."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bp-card">
          <p class="bp-meta">Discipline · 2018</p>
          <h3>Can't Hurt Me</h3>
          <p>"An unflinching account of self-mastery forged in suffering. Not a comfortable read, and not meant to be."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bp-card">
          <p class="bp-meta">Purpose · 1946</p>
          <h3>Man's Search for Meaning</h3>
          <p>"A psychiatrist's testament from the camps: that the last of the human freedoms — to choose one's attitude — cannot be taken away."</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="premise-sub" style="margin-top: 60px; color: rgba(249, 247, 242, 0.6);">Read one book this season — not six. Mark it heavily, return to it often, and let the rest of the shelf wait.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>